{"kind": "finding", "id": "F-recorder-events-004-01", "file": "Source/Parsek.Tests/BackgroundRecorderTests.cs", "line": 1272, "method": "CheckParachuteTransition_WorksWithBackgroundStateCollections", "category": "T2", "severity": "Low", "confidence": "high", "falsifiability": "falsifiability: Source/Parsek/FlightRecorder.cs:1708,1991,3914; break any of the three transitions -> the PartEventTests twin and this copy both red", "what_it_asserts": "That FlightRecorder.CheckParachuteTransition / CheckEngineTransition / CheckDeployableTransition emit the expected PartEventType.", "why_weak": "The three region-9.3 tests construct no BackgroundRecorder and no BackgroundVesselState; they are weaker copies of PartEventTests.ParachuteTransition_StowedToSemiDeployed_EmitsSemiDeployedEvent, EngineTransition_Ignition_EmitsIgnitedEvent and DeployableTransition_RetractedToExtended_EmitsExtendedEvent, so the background-integration claim in the names is never exercised.", "proposed_action": "Delete the three copies, or rewrite one to drive BackgroundRecorder's own polling path over a BackgroundVesselState so the claimed integration is actually covered.", "effort": "S", "july_ref": "none"}
